# Health

Loaded only when a health question arises. Not surfaced in casual briefings.

> **Sensitivity warning:** This file may contain bloodwork, diagnoses, medications, mental health notes. Like `finances.md`, it should never leave your machine. `.gitignore` excludes `memory/` by default.

> **How to populate:** Fill in what you actually track. Skip what you don't. If you have a Google Health (or Whoop / Oura / Apple Health / Garmin) connection, the briefings **auto-update the "Wearable data" sections below** — you only hand-edit the context the wearable can't capture (concerns, doctors, family history, genetic priors). See [`docs/health-system.md`](../docs/health-system.md) for how the four health surfaces work.

